raspi5b: Put RP1 on PCIe2 and add the raspi-cm5 machine

RP1 (hw/misc/rp1.c) is created on PCIe2 at 0002:01:00.0, taking -nic
and the third serial port; its MAC is the one the firmware reports. The
raspi-cm5 machine is a Compute Module 5 on its IO board: board type 0x18,
its model name, and eMMC on SDIO1 in place of the SD card slot. RP1
blocks that are not modelled join the device tree's unmodelled list.
diff --git a/overlay/hw/arm/raspi5b.c b/overlay/hw/arm/raspi5b.c
index 8659e91..9cce8fd 100644
--- a/overlay/hw/arm/raspi5b.c
+++ b/overlay/hw/arm/raspi5b.c
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@
